1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,369
A normal link tells you
how many people clicked.

2
00:00:03,369 --> 00:00:08,212
A trigger link tells you who clicked, and
can start an automation the moment they

3
00:00:08,212 --> 00:00:08,391
do.

4
00:00:08,391 --> 00:00:12,217
In this lesson, you'll create
one, use it, and read the results.

5
00:00:13,071 --> 00:00:16,112
Trigger links live under
Marketing, Trigger Links.

6
00:00:16,112 --> 00:00:20,126
Each one has a name, the web address
it points to, and a link key.

7
00:00:20,126 --> 00:00:22,619
You put the key in your emails and texts,

8
00:00:22,619 --> 00:00:26,086
and Kyntlo turns it into a
tracked link for each contact.

9
00:00:26,936 --> 00:00:30,488
Let's create one for our
November check-up reminder.

10
00:00:30,488 --> 00:00:31,512
Click Add Link.

11
00:00:31,512 --> 00:00:34,244
Give it a name your team will recognise,

12
00:00:34,244 --> 00:00:39,025
then paste the full web address of
the page, including the https part.

13
00:00:39,025 --> 00:00:39,776
Click Save.

14
00:00:40,627 --> 00:00:43,278
Your new link is in the
list, with its own key.

15
00:00:43,278 --> 00:00:43,898
Click Copy.

16
00:00:43,898 --> 00:00:47,846
The key looks a little technical,
but you don't need to understand it.

17
00:00:47,846 --> 00:00:50,948
Just paste it wherever you
would normally paste a link.

18
00:00:51,798 --> 00:00:54,853
Here's our check-up reminder
email in the builder.

19
00:00:54,853 --> 00:00:57,970
Click the button, and in
the website address field,

20
00:00:57,970 --> 00:01:01,086
paste the link key instead
of a normal web address.

21
00:01:01,086 --> 00:01:05,424
You can do the same in text messages,
and in workflow emails and texts.

22
00:01:06,275 --> 00:01:11,464
When the email goes out, every contact gets
their own personal version of that link.

23
00:01:11,464 --> 00:01:16,406
So when Olivia clicks it, Kyntlo knows
it was Olivia, records it on her contact,

24
00:01:16,406 --> 00:01:19,062
and then sends her
straight on to the page.

25
00:01:19,913 --> 00:01:21,667
Here's where it gets powerful.

26
00:01:21,667 --> 00:01:26,402
In Automation, a workflow can start with
the trigger called Trigger Link Clicked.

27
00:01:26,402 --> 00:01:31,312
For example, tag everyone who clicked, and
create a task for your team to call them.

28
00:01:31,312 --> 00:01:34,059
Workflows are part of
the Growth and Pro plans,

29
00:01:34,059 --> 00:01:36,398
and we'll build them in the next module.

30
00:01:37,248 --> 00:01:41,035
Back in Trigger Links, open the
Analyze tab and choose a link.

31
00:01:41,035 --> 00:01:45,860
You'll see total clicks, and unique
clicks, which counts each person only once.

32
00:01:45,860 --> 00:01:48,304
The chart shows which days were busiest.

33
00:01:49,154 --> 00:01:52,065
And here's the real gold:
the people who clicked.

34
00:01:52,065 --> 00:01:53,312
These are warm leads.

35
00:01:53,312 --> 00:01:55,926
They saw your offer and
wanted to know more.

36
00:01:55,926 --> 00:02:00,501
A quick, friendly message to each of
them often turns a click into a booking.

37
00:02:01,351 --> 00:02:06,418
You might wonder how this differs from
the link report in your email statistics.

38
00:02:06,418 --> 00:02:08,445
That report covers one campaign.

39
00:02:08,445 --> 00:02:12,055
A trigger link follows the
same offer across every email,

40
00:02:12,055 --> 00:02:15,918
text and post you use it in,
keeps a history on each contact,

41
00:02:15,918 --> 00:02:17,502
and can start a workflow.

42
00:02:18,352 --> 00:02:19,442
Here's a pro tip.

43
00:02:19,442 --> 00:02:23,802
Create one trigger link per offer,
and use it everywhere: in emails,

44
00:02:23,802 --> 00:02:25,277
texts and social posts.

45
00:02:25,277 --> 00:02:30,663
Then one workflow can follow up with every
interested person, wherever they clicked.

46
00:02:31,516 --> 00:02:33,333
That's the end of Module 8!

47
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:38,448
You can now design emails, send campaigns,
text, post and track every click.

48
00:02:38,448 --> 00:02:42,756
Next, in Module 9, we'll put it
all on autopilot with workflows.

49
00:02:42,756 --> 00:02:43,698
See you there.
